  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "# Issue\n\nStrings (in buttons, tooltips, prompts) for clearing/dismissing notifications have inconsistent and incorrect wording. As there are now group announcements and votings appearing in notification, it is inappropriate to use `Decline` for all messages. `Dismiss` or `Clear` would both be more appropriate. Additionally, inconsistent wording exists through out relevent strings, with words `Decline`, `Dismiss`, `Clear`, `Remove` used mostly interchangeably. (*Fig 1&2*) A consistent word would be much better. Affected strings includes but not limited to:\n\n- `Decline All` 22839\n\n- `Decline all Notifications in currently viewed list.` 13641\n\n- `Clear All` 24121\n\n- `Are you sure you want to remove all notifications?` 34838\n\n- `Are you sure you want to remove all {0} Other notifications?` 34822\n\n- etc.\n\nAlso, why is this one string stuck in Simplified Chinese? (*Fig. 3*) Could be similar problem with the preset messages. Affected string is:\n\n- `Dismisses notification` 17573\n\n# Resolution\n\nI suggest that the `Decline all` wording should be changed to `Dismiss all` or `Clear all`. Generally, `Dismiss` and `Clear` may coexist, and all wording may be decided in case-to-case bases, like `Decline Friend Request`. However, the most general wording should be consistent.",
